course: dictionary
lesson: 4714
title: A word from a famous story
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from stories, and the story helps you understand them. In «Alice in Wonderland», a large blue Caterpillar sits on a mushroom «quietly smoking a long hookah». The words smoking and mushroom are clues, so a hookah must be something you smoke.
explain: A hookah is a tall pipe. Its smoke passes through water in a jar before it is breathed in through a long tube. It is also called a water pipe or shisha. Check the meaning by putting it into the sentence: «The Caterpillar was quietly smoking a long water pipe» still makes sense.
explain: Hookahs come from India, Persia and the Middle East. A dictionary explains what a word means, but it does not make smoking safe. Smoking a hookah is harmful, just as smoking cigarettes is harmful, so never try it.
fact: A hookah is a tall pipe for smoking tobacco.
fact: The smoke of a hookah passes through water in a jar before it is breathed in through a long tube.
fact: A hookah is also called a water pipe or shisha.
fact: Hookahs come from India, Persia and the Middle East.
fact: Smoking a hookah is not safe: it is as harmful as smoking cigarettes, and it is illegal to sell tobacco to children.
exercise: What is a hookah? | A large folded hat | A long blue caterpillar | *A tall pipe for smoking tobacco, with water in it | A kind of mushroom that makes you grow
exercise: Another name for a hookah is a water pipe. What is the other name? | Shiver | Shampoo | Shelter | *Shisha
exercise: Hookahs come from India, Persia and the Middle East. What does this tell you? | Hookahs only grow on mushrooms | *Hookahs have come from places far away, such as India | Hookahs are sold in every school | Hookahs are made from caterpillars
test: Is smoking a hookah safe? | Yes, if you only smoke a little | Yes, it is a safe and healthy habit | *No, it is harmful, as harmful as smoking cigarettes
test: In the story, what does the Caterpillar do with the hookah? | *Smokes it | Puts it in a jar of water to cool | Sells it to Alice | Eats it
exam: What does «hookah» mean, and what is another name for it? | A blue caterpillar in a story | *A tall pipe for smoking tobacco, also called a water pipe or shisha | A jar of water for drinking | A tall tree that grows in India
